cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RocqiPath: whole-slide image processing for computational pathology"
message: >-
  If RocqiPath contributes to published research, please cite it as below,
  together with the underlying software components that were materially used
  in the reported analysis. See CITATION.md for those references.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gajjar
    given-names: Darshil
repository-code: "https://github.com/DarshilGajjar/RocqiPath"
url: "https://github.com/DarshilGajjar/RocqiPath"
abstract: >-
  RocqiPath is a modular Python library for whole-slide image processing in
  computational pathology. It provides slide alignment, WSI and TMA tissue
  extraction, paired patch extraction, stain normalization, chromogen-positive
  cell counting, and visual quality-control tools through typed Python APIs, a
  CLI, and a reproducible study workspace built on physical objective
  magnification.
keywords:
  - computational pathology
  - whole-slide imaging
  - digital pathology
  - image registration
  - stain normalization
  - histopathology
license-url: "https://github.com/DarshilGajjar/RocqiPath/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-04"
